    Q("What is a control chart for?", ["Spotting when a process drifts beyond its normal variation", "Counting employees", "Measuring profit", "Colour-coding samples"], "Points outside the limits signal something has changed."),
    Q("Typical control limits are set at…", ["The mean ± 3 standard deviations", "The mean ± 10%", "The lowest and highest values ever seen", "0 and 100"], "A stable process rarely produces points beyond ±3σ by chance."),
    Q("GMP stands for…", ["Good Manufacturing Practice", "General Measurement Procedure", "Global Market Price", "Good Mixing Protocol"], "Rules covering people, premises, equipment, documents and processes."),
    Q("A method's specificity means it…", ["Measures the analyte without interference from other components", "Is fast", "Is cheap", "Measures everything"], "Impurities and excipients must not distort the result."),
    Q("Stability testing determines…", ["Shelf life and storage conditions", "Colour", "Price", "Dose"], "Samples are stored under defined temperature and humidity and tested over time."),
    Q("An out-of-specification result requires…", ["A documented investigation before any conclusion", "Retesting until it passes", "Quietly discarding it", "Ignoring it"], "'Testing into compliance' is a serious violation."),
    Q("In data integrity, ALCOA stands for…", ["Attributable, Legible, Contemporaneous, Original, Accurate", "Always Label Chemicals Or Assays", "Assay, Limit, Control, Output, Audit", "Analyse, Log, Check, Order, Approve"], "Records must show who did what, when, in the original form."),
